#### E.1 Predicting verification labels

Following prior work [\(Snell et al.,](#page-11-9) [2024;](#page-11-9) [Beeching et al.\)](#page-9-4), we aggregate scores from DiscPRM by using the score of the *last* step. For THINKPRM, we first prompt the model to generate the verification chain up to a maximum of 8192 tokens, then we force decode the string *"Is the solution correct?"* and use <sup>P</sup> ("yes") P ("yes")+P ("no") as the solution score.

